# Engine traps

Each of these has already burned time on this project. Full write-up in
[docs/engine-notes.md](mdc:docs/engine-notes.md).

## A node-typed `@export` never resolves in a hand-authored `.tscn`

`map = NodePath("../World/Map")` leaves the property **null**. The Godot editor
stores extra state that a text-authored scene does not have.

Use a `NodePath` export resolved through `scripts/node_ref.gd`, which names the node
and the field when a path is bad. The editor still shows a node picker.

## `Control.set_anchors_preset()` does not size a control

It sets anchors, then adjusts offsets so the rectangle does not move — and a fresh
control has a **zero-sized** rectangle. Use `InkUi.fill_parent()`, which calls
`set_anchors_and_offsets_preset()`.

The failure is asymmetric, which is why it survives review:

- `ScrollContainer` **clips** → screen goes blank, you notice immediately.
- Plain `Control` **does not clip** → it draws its contents while every anchor inside collapses onto the origin. Looks fine, is wrong.

## `modulate` multiplies — black art cannot be tinted lighter

- Art from `assets/` is drawn in final ink colours and takes **no tint**.
- Hand-authored art (`cargo_body`, `cargo_rider`, `barrier`) is drawn in **white** and tinted at runtime.

The white-plus-tint convention is what lets one file serve both the damage flash
(§13.2) and the light grey dead marks (§15.11). `InkSprite` supports both;
`assets/README.md` records which file is which.

## Convex decomposition fails on a repeated vertex

A zone offset that is a round number can land exactly on a route sample offset,
giving the polygon a duplicate vertex and a zero-length edge. `Map._band_polygon`
compares strictly. Expect this for any new zone authored at a round offset.

## The navigation bake is sensitive to outline density

Offsetting all 227 road samples by 570 px put many outline vertices in one
rasterisation cell → **39 edge-merge errors**. Offsetting a decimated 200 px spine
and snapping the outline to whole pixels brought it to **3 warnings**, which remain
and are owned by milestone 2.

## Screenshots must run windowed

`--write-movie` crashes under `--headless`; saving a viewport image needs a real
rendering device. `tools/screenshot_run.tscn` runs windowed on purpose.
